{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he dwelt in the wilderness.</b> Therefore they called him פרא אדם (a wild ass of a man)." "<b>And he became a great archer.</b> One may say it is from the root רביא. That is, <b>and he became</b> — Ishmael was a lad — <b>an archer</b> shooting arrows; אנפנ״ט in Old French, ארקי״ר."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The Old French glosses are rendered as transcribed; אנפנ״ט and ארקי״ר likely correspond to OF *archier* (archer) or related terms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:10.540254119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}